        "thinking": "Now I understand the issue. The `RunLogHandle` type in `server/src/services/run-log-store.ts` is:\n```ts\nexport type RunLogStoreType = \"local_file\";\nexport interface RunLogHandle {\n  store: RunLogStoreType; // = \"local_file\"\n  logRef: string;\n}\n```\n\nBut the R2 implementation in `packages/deploy-cloudflare/src/storage/r2-run-log-store.ts` imports these types and tries to use `store: \"r2\"`. Since the type says `store: \"local_file\"`, comparing it to `\"r2\"` is a type error.\n\n\nThe solution is to have the R2 log store define its own handle type with `store: \"r2\"` instead of trying to reuse the server's `RunLogHandle` type. I need to check both the R2 run log store and workspace operation log store implementations, and also look at how `R2Provider` relates to the `StorageProviderFactory` type in `boot.ts`.\n\nFor the other issues: `hyperdrive.ts` needs postgres added as a dependency, and once I remove the exclude from the worker API configuration, the module resolution errors should clear up, though there may still be some implicit any and type issues to address.",
        "type": "thinking"
      }
